alse,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":344,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:11:11Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-23T22:00:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T19:42:53Z","closed_at":"2026-08-26T19:39:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122751","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122751","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122751.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122751.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-26T19:39:27Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Supersedes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122727\r\n- Follow-up of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122596\r\n\r\nReduces RAM usage of the editor by ~13mb.\r\nThis was done in follow-up to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122596, where a ~25mb increase was deemed acceptable for the performance improvement. This PR brings it back down by ~13mb (to around +12mb net plus).\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe reduction was achieved by consolidating _all_ property information into a single map (or rather, one self + one aggregated) such that keyvalues are deduplicated.\r\n\r\nAs a side benefit (or if I'm being honest, perhaps the main benefit long term), the new code makes it structurally impossible to have colliding property names, which decreases the risk of bugs as this code evolves or is used.\r\nIt's also arguably more predictable, since all properties are accessed in the same way.\r\n\r\nThis also fixes a regression from earlier GDType PRs where disabled classes' methods are not hidden as expected.\r\n\r\nEnums are now also part of an object's namespace: `Object.Enum.Value` resolves, so clearly `Object` claims the member `Enum`. Since enums are not types, there's nothing logical to return, but it IS handled in the same way that other non-existing namespaces are (e.g. `Object.property` when `property` has no getter is also handled, though notably without erroring (which is also kind of odd)).\r\n\r\n### Tests \r\n\r\nI tested the RAM decrease with the test from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122596.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_i